course: dictionary
lesson: 11960
title: Castanets: a word from music and dance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. Read the clues. «Mia held a pair of castanets and clicked them in time with the music.» Mia holds them, clicks them and plays along to music, so castanets must be a small musical instrument.
explain: «The dancer's castanets made a sharp rhythm as she stepped across the stage.» A rhythm is a pattern of beats, and sharp tells you the sound was clear and quick. Check it: swap in "her small drums made a sharp rhythm" and the sentence still works, so you are on the right track.
explain: Stories often use words to paint a picture. «The Spanish dancers clicked their castanets as the guitar began to play.» Spain, guitar and dancers all point to flamenco, a style of dance from Spain. When a word is new, ask what the words around it show you.
fact: Castanets are a small musical instrument.
fact: «Castanets» are two shell-shaped pieces of hard wood or plastic, held in the hand.
fact: You click the two pieces together to make a sharp rhythm.
fact: Castanets are often used in Spanish dancing and flamenco.
fact: One castanet is one piece; a pair of castanets is two pieces.
exercise: «Ruby clicked the castanets together to keep the beat.» What are castanets? | A type of Spanish soup | A kind of dance shoe | *A small instrument you click together by hand | A large drum played with sticks
exercise: «The flamenco dancer's castanets sounded sharp and bright.» Which dance style are castanets most often linked with? | *Flamenco | Cooking in the kitchen | Ballet on a frozen lake | Football matches
exercise: «The castanets made a sharp rhythm.» Find and copy the word that means a pattern of beats. | sharp | *rhythm | made | castanets
test: «Tom held a pair of castanets in his right hand.» How many pieces are in a pair? | Three | Four | One | *Two
test: «Ella clicked the castanets to keep the beat in the music lesson.» What are castanets used for here? | To paint a picture | To cook a meal | *To keep the beat | To wash the stage
exam: «The dancers stamped their feet and played castanets.» What do you do to castanets to make them sound? | *Click them together | Blow into them | Shake them | Stir them
